{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "At the Clothing Store"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Best Buy"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > World of Food > Pronunciation"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately exchange information about buying things in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Stressing information in sentences - Expressing Likes and Dislikes"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You add emphasis or stress to the words in a sentence that are the most important. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can change the word you stress if another word is more important, such as a like or dislike. Stressed words can also be adjectives like <span class = \"italic\">big, difficult and very.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: I <span class = \"strong\">don't</span> like that shirt. <span class = \"strong\">The word \"don't\" is stressed</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"italic\\\">I <span class = \\\"strong\\\">like</span> my new sweater and sunglasses.</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class = \\\"strong\\\">adore</span> everything in that store.</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class = \\\"strong\\\">love</span> your new jacket and tie. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Dislikes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"italic\\\">He <span class = \\\"strong\\\">doesn't</span> like shopping very much.</span><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I really <span class = \\\"strong\\\">don't</span> like shopping.</span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">I <span class = \\\"strong\\\">hate</span> waiting in line.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an experience, moment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am having a good time at the party."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le07ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk about shopping."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to buy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to pay for something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I buy a lot of gifts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le07ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "kind"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "nice, gentle"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That was very kind of you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le07ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to like"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to enjoy doing something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I like everything in that store."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le07ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tie"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an accessory you wear around your neck"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:I love your new jacket and tie."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le07ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "belonging to you"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(pronoun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are like mine."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le07ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to suit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look good on someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Those sunglasses suit you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le07ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le07ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Long i Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "To make the Long i sound: </br></br>Step 1: First, move your tongue towards your bottom teeth so it sits low in the mouth. </br> Step 2: Close your jaw slightly and move your tongue upward until it is near the top of your mouth, behind your teeth. </br></br>This is similar to the position of a y sound.</br> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Long i Sound in Words"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Spelling \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"igh\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"night, fight, light\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"i_e\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nice, spice, rice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ie\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pie, tie, die\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-y\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ply, sky, dry\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-y-\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cycle, dynamic\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Put the words with the long <span class=\"italic\">i</span> sound in alphabetical order."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say these words out loud with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find 5 new words with the long <span class=\"italic\">i</span> sound on the Internet or in a dictionary. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Add them to the list."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Words\\\"}\",